<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Grammar agreement ~ the second condition of belonging

''A node belongs to a Nexus by CONTRACT and by AGREEING WITH THE GRAMMAR VECTORS traded there.'' A node that cannot read what a Nexus trades cannot carry it faithfully, cannot verify what it relays, and cannot be bound by what it never parsed — //contract without grammar-agreement reads as a signature over an unread page//.

''This meme held a TODO naming a source file that never existed in this repo's history.'' It stands as GROUND rather than design: what the field already proved, gathered so the design lands on it instead of re-deriving it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-outside-art>>

!! What the field proved ~ and the one mechanism that held

''THE SHAPE IS DEPLOYED, and its two checks sit as ADJACENT BULLETS.'' MLS (RFC 9420 §7.3, LeafNode validation) lists credential-valid and signature-valid, then compatibility-with-group-parameters and required-extensions-listed-in-capabilities. ''A peer passing the first pair and failing the second is rejected from the group while remaining perfectly authentic.'' Exactly the two conditions, textually apart, in a protocol shipping at consumer scale.

''★ AGREEMENT IS KEYED, NEVER AUDITED ★'' — and this reads as the load-bearing find. RFC 9420 §12.1.7 folds the declared grammar into the key schedule by way of the `confirmation_tag`: ''disagree on the grammar and you derive a different key and fail to decrypt.'' The reason matters more than the mechanism — ''you cannot detect a peer that LIES about understanding'', so MLS never asks. It makes the lie non-computable. Twenty-four years of the alternative stand recorded: the same //declared-critical-and-simply-not-processed// bug shipping in 2002, 2011 and 2026, across three vendors.

''EXCLUSION POWER IS BOUNDED BY THE EXCLUDER'S MARKET SHARE.'' Three fields built this gate correctly and three retreated under deployment pressure — the X.509 criticality MUST suspended by ballot; SOAP's `mustUnderstand` answered by //just ignore those//; BGP replacing session-reset with ignore (RFC 5492). ''MLS held because it gates at the GROUP boundary'', where the members are the whole relevant population and the roster stays local. So the gate reads deployable at ''Lararium and Nexus'' scale and predicts the same retreat at ''DreamNet'' scale — which lands exactly on the standing no-roster ruling, since a bilateral contract per operator keeps the check bilateral and peer-local.

''ActivityPub FORBIDS this gate rather than lacking it'' (AS2-Core §5: a consumer MUST NOT stop processing or signal an error on unfamiliar extensions). So the check cannot live conformantly on that vocabulary; it lives in a layer we own.

!!! Four constraints any build inherits

# ''Tell the peer WHICH term it lacked.'' SOAP's `NotUnderstood` names the failing header; MLS rejects silently. The feedback costs almost nothing and turns an exclusion into an upgrade prompt.
# ''Ship the lockout preview BEFORE the tighten.'' Matrix descoped exactly that query — an operator raising a room version cannot see who they are about to lock out — and has carried the debt for a decade.
# ''Tier the vocabulary.'' COSE `crit` (RFC 9052 §3.1) marks only the unlikely-to-be-known labels as must-understand; the common ones stay out. That tiering is the structural cure for the retreat above.
# ''The check is a PARSER on untrusted input at the admission boundary — fuzz it.'' The comprehension-checking code has itself been the vulnerability repeatedly, including a name-constraint checker that was the buffer overflow and a flag requesting stricter checking that destroyed the check it strengthened.

''And any ignore-unknown clause rusts shut unless traffic proves otherwise'' — GREASE (RFC 8701) exists because implementations that reject unknown values interoperate fine with today's peers, so the mistake spreads unnoticed until the joint has seized. TLS 1.3 pays that debt permanently, impersonating 1.2 on the wire forever.

— outside art, verified against primary sources; ''the design that sits on it stays the operator's'', and a prior treatment exists on another worldline to surface from the sensorium.

<<~/ahu>>

